6.2   Scoring based on the EWM-TOPSIS
   The Entropy Weight Method (EWM) is an objective approach for determining the




                                                      学
weights of multiple indicators. It utilizes the concept of information entropy to cal-
culate the weight of each indicator. TOPSIS (Technique for Order of Preference by
Similarity to Ideal Solution) is a multi-criteria decision analysis method used to deter-




                                                    数
mine the best choice by comparing the similarity of each alternative to the ideal and
worst solutions. In this context, we use the EWM method to assign weights to each in-
                                                 ：
dicator and then apply the TOPSIS method to assess the conservation value of different
locations.




